{title: 654 - Lord, Bless Our Homes}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #654 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 654}
{meta: category Christian Home - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Lord, [F]bless [Gm]our [Am]homes [Bb]with [Gm]peace [Am]and [F]love [Dm]and laughter,
[C]With understanding [Am]and [C]with [Am]loyalty.
[Gm]May we together [Dm]follow [F]Christ [Gm]the [Am]Master
[Edim]And [F]know [Gm]the [Am]blessing [C]of [Am]His [F]sov'reignty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]May [F]every heart [Bb]receive [Am]His [F]loving [Dm/F]spirit
[C]And know the truth [F]that [Am]makes [C]life [Am]truly [Gm]free;
[Gm]Then, in that [Bb]spirit [Dm]may [Edim]we [F]live [Gm]united,
[Edim]And [F]find [Gm]in [Am]God [C]our deep [Am]security.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Forgive [Gm]the [Am]hurts [Bb]our [Am]selfishness [Dm]inflicted
[C]On whose we [F]love and [Am]those [C]who love [Am]us [Gm]best.
[Gm]Christ, heal the [Bb]scars [Am]and [Dm]draw [Edim]us [F]all [Gm]together
[Edim]In [F]Him [Gm]whose [Am]will [C]is peace [Am]and [F]joy [Gm]and [Am]rest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Father, [Gm]in [Am]gratitude [Gm]for [Am]homes [Dm]and loved [Edim]one,
[C]We open [F]now our [Am]hearts [C]to all [Am]mankind.
[Gm]Grand us Your [Bb]spirit [Dm]love [Edim]for [F]one [Gm]another
[Edim]So [F]in [Gm]Your [Am]peace [C]may we [Am]our [F]concord [Am]find.
{end_of_verse}
